From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +000
Subject: [PATCH] lib/replace: use C23 memset_explicit signature

glibc 2.43 exposes the C23 memset_explicit() API, which takes three
arguments:

  memset_explicit(void *dest, int ch, size_t len)

libreplace's rep_memset_s() wrapper already validates the destination
size and count before calling memset_explicit(), so pass the same
arguments used by the memset() fallback.

Upstream: Not submitted
Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
---
 lib/replace/replace.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lib/replace/replace.c b/lib/replace/replace.c
index 5f2879fb6e5a..6e4327d348f2 100644
--- a/lib/replace/replace.c
+++ b/lib/replace/replace.c
@@ -970,7 +970,7 @@ int rep_memset_s(void *dest, size_t destsz, int ch, size_t count)
 	}
 
 #if defined(HAVE_MEMSET_EXPLICIT)
-	memset_explicit(dest, destsz, ch, count);
+	memset_explicit(dest, ch, count);
 #else /* HAVE_MEMSET_EXPLICIT */
 	memset(dest, ch, count);
 # if defined(HAVE_GCC_VOLATILE_MEMORY_PROTECTION)
-- 
2.50.0

